  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "tXCP0UOigUsc0jKhgvO/4+qdeQI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:08.116Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The upgrade runs exactly **once**, when `UPGRADE_DOCUMENT` is dispatched. Replay never re-runs it: loading a document (`baseLoadFromInput` \u2192 `replayDocument`) starts from the stored `initialState` and folds the domain operations through the latest reducer. The `document`-scope log where the upgrade was recorded is not part of that fold.\n\nThat asymmetry is the whole trap. A migration that patches `state` but forgets `initialState` produces a document that looks perfectly healthy in the running system \u2014 and is unrecoverable:\n\n- anything seeded into `initialState`, i.e. data that was never created by an operation, is still v1-shaped there;\n- so a rebuild can no longer reproduce the stored state;\n- so the replayed final state fails the recorded hash check.\n\nThe document then errors on load with a `HashMismatchError` whose message embeds `Hash mismatch on document \u2026, scope global`. The recipe's tests match it with `/Hash mismatch/`.\n\nThe failure mode is worth dwelling on: nothing goes wrong at upgrade time, nothing goes wrong while the process stays up, and the break surfaces later on a cold load or on a peer that never held the live document. The `document-versioning` recipe ships a deliberately broken state-only transition specifically so the failure is visible in a test rather than in production.\n\nTwo supporting constraints from the same recipe. Upgrade reducers **must be pure** \u2014 they run on every peer that loads the document, so no `Date.now()`, no randomness, no I/O \u2014 and they must **return** a new document spread-style, because there is no immer/Mutative draft in an upgrade reducer and in-place mutation is simply lost. And `supportedVersions` is ordered and every hop must be covered: upgrading a v1 document on a package already at v3 composes v1\u2192v2 then v2\u2192v3, with a missing intermediate entry throwing at upgrade time.\n\nProvenance: academy `05-Lookup/00-Cookbook.md`, Document Versioning recipe (\"Critical pitfall: patch state and initialState together\"), academy 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:39:07.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:08.116Z"
    }
  },
